OL,3,GNEWSAPolice expand use of facial
OL,4,Arecognition technology
OL,5,
OL,6,FPolice have used live facial
OL,7,Frecognition (LFR) for the first time in
OL,8,FDevon.
OL,10,FThe technology, which scans faces in
OL,11,Fcrowds from a live camera feed and
OL,12,Fchecks them against a watchlist of
OL,13,Fwanted people, was used in Exmouth town
OL,14,Fcentre at the end of August, officers
OL,15,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,345,340,200,160,0,100
PN,34402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F344A1788855940
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSAPolice expand use of facial
OL,4,Arecognition technology
OL,5,
OL,6,FSgt Angela Galasso, from Devon and
OL,7,FCornwall Police, said the technology
OL,8,Fwas probably "scanning far more faces
OL,9,Fthan a police officer ever could",
OL,10,Fadding: "It's a tool. One of the many
OL,11,Fin our armour which help us to do our
OL,12,Fjob."
OL,14,FAny people identified by LFR still
OL,15,Fneeded to be verified by humans, police
OL,16,Fsaid. Human rights group Liberty has
OL,17,Fcalled for legislation to clarify how
OL,18,Fpolice forces can use such systems.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
